:: OC Micah Nature Hike 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
You walk towards the entrance to the woods, happy and excited to spend this school-free day exploring the great outdoors, when you stumble upon <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> standing near the entrance. <span style="color:Yellow">He is alone, but is pacing back and forth while mumbling to himself. He looks a little stressed and unsure.</span> You get a bit closer to try and hear what he is talking about. 

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "OC Micah",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Eyes: "Sad",
            Blush: 2,
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Frown",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Come on, you can do this! Just a little walk, it’ll be relaxing!”</span> He is trying to hype himself up, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Just don’t think about getting kidnapped or silenced or abducted, well actually abducted wouldn’t be the worst thing – if it’s aliens. Because at least that will FINALLY prove me right! Aahhhh~! But if I get abducted who will cover my shift at the shop? Oh man, maybe this isn’t such a good idea.”</span> The boy seems to be in a crisis. A very strange and unrealistic crisis, but one none-the-less! So, you walk up and greet him, hoping to be able to help. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Aahh! Don’t abduct me yet, I’m still needed!”</span> The boy holds up his hands in fear, before opening his eyes and realizing it is just you. He then turns bright red, realizing what he just said. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh, ummm… <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>… When did…? H- how much of that did you hear?”</span> You tell him you heard enough. Is there a reason he is pacing around mumbling about being abducted? <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“It’s just…”</span> He sighs, plopping down on a nearby bench with his face in his hands. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Last time I was here I found this really cool, relaxing spot with a GREAT view of the mountains – where there is obviously a secret government base – and I planned on going over there to relax and take a look. But then I realized that if I was going to get abducted by aliens, it would be in a corn field OR the woods! And I’m covering the shop for my grandparents later so if I get abducted then-!”</span> <br>
<br>
The boy begins to ramble. You understand next to nothing, other than aliens possibly trying to shut down or sabotage his family’s establishment. Feeling your head starting to hurt, you offer to join the boy in his woodlands adventure. After all, most people who get taken by aliens are conveniently free of other witnesses, right? <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Exactly!”</span> He pops up excitedly, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“They normally go after solo-players. So, we should be fine on our own… unless they’ve recently changed their methods…”</span> You quickly grab him by the arm and drag him into the woods before he starts to overthink things again. <br>
<br>
<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> is still extremely nervous during the hike, but having you around makes him a little bit less. If he were by himself, you’re pretty sure he’d be curled up in a ball under a tree or something. Instead, he seems mostly normal outside of stopping occasionally to spout fun facts about various plants or insects you see. <span style="color:LightGreen">The kid is pretty knowledgeable about biology and nature. It’s pretty enduring to see him ramble about.</span>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "OC Micah",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

    Eventually you reach the hill near the river that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> was talking about. It is a bit of a hike up, one of which the young and feeble <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> is not suited for, <span style="color:LightGreen">but with your help he is able to reach the top and gasps out at the wonderful view.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Wow!”</span> He says with a big smile. <span style="color:LightGreen">This really is a great view, to be fair,</span> as the hill crusts just above most of the trees and lets you get a wonderful view of the snow-tipped mountains further to the north of town. To the west, you can even see the ocean in all its blue glory. This is quite the spot! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> pulls out some binoculars and begins to peer towards the mountains. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Hmmm… not seeing the spying scope anywhere. They must have improved their camouflage technology. If I remember correctly it was…”</span> He begins to mumble to himself and take notes. The boy is truly invested in these conspiracies of his. You decide to take a seat and admire the view until he is done with whatever research he is conducting. <br>
    <br>
    After about 10 minutes, he is finished and walks up to you with a shy smile. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Sorry for making you wait, I kind of forgot you were here… sorry…”</span> He reaches down and helps you up, giving an apologetic look but you say it’s alright. The view was really worth the trip! You thank him for bringing you here and, to lighten the mood, you ask him some questions about these theories of his on the way back. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:Pink">You regret your decision almost immediately, but it is cute how confident he is.</span> <br>
    <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
    <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
    <<socialChange "Micah" 3 1>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|Wald Street]]
<</linkreplace>>